Article 9: The central finance shall implement compensation for units and individuals that carry out protection of important ecological and environmental elements according to the following categories (hereinafter referred to as categorized compensation):
(1) forests;
(2) grasslands;
(3) wetlands;
(4) deserts;
(5) oceans;
(6) watercourses;
(7) cultivated land;
(8) other important ecological and environmental elements such as aquatic biological resources, terrestrial wild animals and plant resources as specified by laws, administrative regulations, and State provisions.
The specific scope and methods of compensation as provided in the preceding paragraph shall be determined by category after taking into comprehensive consideration factors such as the regional economic and social development level, financial affordability, and ecological protection effectiveness, and shall be publicly announced to the society according to law together with matters such as the use of compensation funds and their supervision and management. The specific measures for central fiscal categorized compensation shall be formulated by the competent department of the State Council in conjunction with other relevant departments by field.

Article 15 Inter-regional horizontal ecological protection compensation shall be conducted in the following areas:
(1) Areas along the upper and lower reaches, left and right banks, and main and tributary streams of river basins;
(2) Areas where important ecological and environmental elements are located and other areas with significant ecological functions;
(3) Water source areas of major water diversion projects and the protection zones along their routes;
(4) Other areas where ecological protection compensation is conducted under agreements.

Article 17 For conducting inter-regional horizontal ecological protection compensation, the relevant local people's governments shall enter into a written agreement (hereinafter referred to as the compensation agreement) specifying the following matters:
(1) The specific scope of compensation;
(2) The expected targets of ecological protection and the indicators for monitoring and evaluation thereof;
(3) The ecological protection responsibilities of the ecological protection area;
(4) The methods of compensation and the relevant arrangements for implementing the compensation;
(5) The term of the agreement;
(6) The handling of violations of the agreement;
(7) Other matters.
In determining the content of the compensation agreement, factors such as the current status of ecological protection, the cost of ecological protection, the effectiveness of ecological protection, the level of regional economic and social development, and fiscal affordability shall be comprehensively considered.
The ecological protection compensation funds obtained by the ecological protection area shall be used for the protection of natural resources, management and restoration of the ecological environment, economic and social development, and improvement of people's livelihood in that area. Where compensation needs to be directly provided to units and individuals, it shall be made in a timely manner in accordance with the provisions, and shall not be intercepted, occupied, misappropriated or defaulted.
